From 0cd84fc809e3e5c5cd4d7ee243f11f1ade3a3dc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 01:20:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(setup): place a setup relative to another; transform
 between setups

One rigid transform per setup: the #326 part alignment. The transform
from setup A to setup B is derived from the two alignments
(setup_relative::transform_between, T = A_B * A_A^-1), refusing a
missing setup, a non-setup and a non-rigid stored alignment by name.

A setup may now be placed relative to another (SetupDef::relative_to,
SetSetupRelative::link / unlink): "flip over X / turn 90 about Z / typed
angles from <setup>" resolves into the setup's part alignment through
AlignPartToSetup, so the stock follows as in #326. A later change of the
parent's alignment re-places every linked setup (transitively) in the
same undo unit, keeping its transform to the parent, or refuses the
whole change naming the setup that cannot follow. Self links and loops
are refused; DeleteSetup refuses a parent. Datum transfer does not link
(a clone, not an alias); nothing is read from the work offset.

Project v56: SetupDto::relative_to (absent = not linked); a link to no
setup or a loop of links is a corrupt file. The setup page offers
"Relative to previous setup". Decisions: docs/decisions/316-setup-transform.md.

Fixes #316

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
